




			    CE6 Programming Manual
				  Version 2.1


	 The CE6 (Clone/Editor 6) is used to program the VX-500V and
    VX-500U series radios.  The radio is connected to the computer by
    the VPL-1 and appropriate cable.  To start the program, type the
    following at the DOS prompt:

	 C:>CE6

	 The program will display the version number and frequency ranges
    for different model of radio then goes to main channel data screen.

	 The main channel data screen will allow you to enter all of the
    channel and tone data as well as set some of the programmable options
    like CTCSS, Time Out Timer, etc.  You can also access all of the other
    functions from the main screen by pressing one of the 'F' keys:

	 F1:  On-line help
	 F2:  Common Data/Hardware Setup
	 F3:  Load a file from disk
	 F4:  Save a file to disk
	 F5:  Read data from a radio
	 F6:  Send data to a radio
	 F7:  Print out configuration
	 F8:  Return to DOS
	 F9:  Change radio type/model

	 The program starts with the default setting for VX-500V.  To
    change the radio type use the F9 key and select the radio type.
    Changing types will erase any previous data on the screen.

	 Two information boxes appear at the top of the screen.  The left
    box contains information about the common data and radio configuration.
    The box on the right contains key help information for data entry such
    as which keys to use and the upper and lower limits for data.


	 Before programming the channel data, make sure that the COMMON
    DATA and ENVIRONMENT settings are correct. The following items can be
    entered from the channel data menu:

    PRIORITY CHANNEL-One channel can be enabled as a priority; use the
    <SPACE> bar to select.

    CHANNEL NAME-This is the 4 digit alpha tag assigned to the channel
    number.  Any character from A-Z, 0-9, and <=>*+-\/_<space> may be
    entered.  The default tags are CH01 to CH32.  If DTMF TAG is selected
    under COMMON DATA, this will be the DTMF encode/decode sequence.  Press
    the <SPACE> bar to toggle between off, encode only, or encode decode
    (displayed with "T" as the 4th digit).



				       1










    RX FREQ-Enter any frequency within the selected range (134-174 for VHF
    400-512 for UHF) and channel spacing.  Pressing the <SPACE> bar will
    toggle the "channel lock" on or off; if locked, the channel data will
    not be displayed or accessed by the user, but will still be downloaded.

    CTCSS/DCS Decode-Press <ENTER> to select the tone/code frequency from a
    pop up table, or enter the tone/code directly.  Pressing <SPACE>
    toggles the sub-audible selection on/off.

    SCAN-Press the <SPACE> bar to change the scan list selection for this
    channel.

    POWER SAVE-Press the <SPACE> bar to toggle battery saver on/off.  The
    on/off times can be altered under COMMON DATA.

    TX FREQ-Enter any frequency within the selected range (134-174 for VHF
    400-512 for UHF) and channel spacing.  Pressing the <SPACE> bar will
    toggle the channel between receive only and TX/RX.

    CTCSS/DCS Encode-Press <ENTER> to select the tone/code frequency from a
    pop up table, or enter the tone/code directly.  Pressing <SPACE>
    toggles the sub-audible selection on/off.

    BCLO/BTLO-Press the <SPACE> bar to toggle between Busy Tone Lock Out,
    Busy Carrier Lock Out, and None.  BTLO will inhibit the transmitter if
    carrier is detected but the correct tone is not decoded.  BCLO will
    inhibit the transmitter anytime carrier is detected.

    TX POWER-Press the <SPACE> bar to toggle the channel between low power
    only, or HI/LO power (selectable by the user).

    TOT-Press the <SPACE> bar to toggle the TX Time Out Timer on/off. The
    timer duration is set under COMMON DATA.

    COMMON DATA

    Pressing <F2> will allow you to view/edit the radio common data.  All
    of the selections are altered using the <SPACE> bar.  The following
    items can be accessed from this menu:

    1.   Channel scan enable or disable.  If enabled, items 2 & 3 may be
	 selected.

    2.   Scan Stop Resume- Select either 5 Sec or CARRIER.  If set to
	 CARRIER, scan will resume 2 Sec after carrier drops.  If set to 5
         Sec, scan will pause only for that time, then resume regardless of
	 activity.

    3.   User Scan Program- If enabled, the user will be able select the
         scan channels by pressing the DW/S button while turning power on.





				       2










    4.   Dual Watch- Enables or disables the dual watch feature.  If
	 enabled the radio will sample the priority channel for activity
	 when receiving a non-priority channel.  If this feature is enabled
	 the  next 2 items may be selected.

    5.   Power-On dual watch- If enabled, the radio will be in the dual
         watch mode as soon as the power is turned on.

    6.   Dual watch speed- Slow will sample the priority channel at 1.5
         second intervals; Fast will sample at .5 second intervals.

    7.   Channel after PTT- Select either Home, Last Busy or Priority.
         When the PTT is pressed during scan, this is the channel that the
         radio will revert to.  Home is the last channel selected before
	 entering scan.

    8.   Monitor- The monitor button on the side panel of the radio may
         be enabled or disabled using this selection.

    9.   Beep- The key beeps when pressing any of the radio buttons (except
         PTT) may be enabled or disabled using this selection.

    10.  Lighting Lock- The key lock may be enabled or disabled using this
         selection.  If enabled, and the user presses the lighting/lock
         button on the side panel, all of the buttons (except PTT and the
	 channel selector) will be disabled until another long press of
         the button.

    11.  Power Save- Select the sleep time of the power save mode.  To
         select the awake time, see ENVIRONMENT.

    12.  TX Time Out- Select either enabled or disabled. If enabled, the
         next 2 items may be selected.

    13.  TX Time Out Time- Select either 30 Sec, 1 min, 2 min, or 3 min.

    14.  Time Out Resume is the amount of penalty time that must expire
         before the user can transmit again if they have exceeded the TOT.
         Select either 0, 6, 20, or 60 Sec.

    15   Squelch Tail Elimination- If enabled and CTCSS is programmed,
	 releasing the PTT button will cause the radio to continue to
         transmit for 400 mSec without tone to eliminate the squelch tail
         on the receiving end.

    16.  The "A" and "B" option buttons may be programmed for any of the
         following: Change group (moves between channels 1-16 and 17-32)
	 Hi/Lo transmit power, Talkaround, channel alpha/number display,
         or Accessory.

    17.  DTMF Sel Call/Ch Name- Toggles between displaying the channel
         number/name and the DTMF decode/encode sequence.



                                       3










    18.  Power on Display- Select either channel number or channel alpha
         tag.  This option will also be dependent upon the selection of
         item 17.

    19.  2-Tone Decoder- Select either groups 1,2,3/4,5,6 or custom tone.
	 This option is used in conjunction with the F2D-5 2-Tone Decoder.

    SERIAL PORT

    Pressing <F4> in the COMMON DATA screen will allow you to change serial
    port if computer has more than one serial port.

    ENVIRONMENT

    The following items can be displayed by pressing <F2> while in the
    COMMON DATA menu.  Only the default split may be edited, and is pro-
    vided as a programming aid.

    1.   Prescalar-  1/64 (default).

    2.   Channel step- Default depends on radio type.

    3.   1st IF Freq- Default depends on radio type.

    4.   Local Osc Offset- Default depends on radio type.

    5.   Default split is applied to the receive frequency to automatically
	 calculate the transmit frequency.  This setting does not affect
	 the operation of the radio.

    6.   Scan Speed- 150mSec/channel (default).

    7.   Power Save time- 300 mSec.  This will determine how long the radio
	 is "awake" during the power save mode to check for activity.

	 To return to the COMMON DATA menu press <ESC>

    TONE

	 The 2-Tone and Burst Tone entries may be accessed  by pressing
    <F3> while in the COMMON DATA menu. 2-Tone Decode and Burst Tone are
    mutually exclusive functions since they both require an option board.
    Enter the tone frequency in directly, or select from a pop up menu if
    the wrong data is entered.  Pressing the <SPACE> bar will toggle the
    selection on/off.

	 To return to the COMMON DATA menu press <ESC>













